<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>HaulTimes</title><link>https://haultimes.com/</link><description>Freight and trucking news for the US and Canada</description><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:11:54 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Fleets commit to hiring 13K vets through &#x27;Freedom Haulers&#x27; program</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fleets-commit-to-hiring-13k-vets-through-freedom-haulers-program-c09dcdd12b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fleets-commit-to-hiring-13k-vets-through-freedom-haulers-program-c09dcdd12b/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:12:59 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Atlanta Rapper Hunxho Unveils Fleet of Semi-Trucks After Launching Trucking Business</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/atlanta-rapper-hunxho-unveils-fleet-of-semi-trucks-after-launching-tru-16b50bcbe8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/atlanta-rapper-hunxho-unveils-fleet-of-semi-trucks-after-launching-tru-16b50bcbe8/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:43:35 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Hypefresh Magazine, Inc.</description></item><item><title>Second fatal commercial vehicle crash on Highway 69 in 8 days</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/second-fatal-commercial-vehicle-crash-on-highway-69-in-8-days-e7d0f68271/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/second-fatal-commercial-vehicle-crash-on-highway-69-in-8-days-e7d0f68271/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>CTV News</description></item><item><title>Bipartisan bill to require truck driver bathroom access at shippers and receivers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/bipartisan-bill-to-require-truck-driver-bathroom-access-at-shippers-an-23f1039fed/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/bipartisan-bill-to-require-truck-driver-bathroom-access-at-shippers-an-23f1039fed/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:07:40 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Two senators from opposite parties, Deb Fischer (R-Neb.) and Lisa Blunt Rochester (D-Del.), introduced the Trucker Bathroom Access Bill on November 12, 2026, and a companion version was introduced in the House. If passed, the measure would give drivers picking up or delivering freight the same restroom access as a business’s customers or employees, at shippers, receivers, manufacturers, warehouses and distribution centers. The bill would not require businesses to build new restroom facilities. Several trucking groups have endorsed it, including the Owner-Operator Independent Drivers Association, the American Trucking Association, Women in Trucking Association, She Trucking and Trinity Logistics.</description></item><item><title>Data shows serial noncompliance behind majority of ELD revocations</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/data-shows-serial-noncompliance-behind-majority-of-eld-revocations-43b518a5f1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/data-shows-serial-noncompliance-behind-majority-of-eld-revocations-43b518a5f1/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:56:28 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Orange County Teamsters say have ratified contract, will end 24-day strike</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/orange-county-teamsters-say-have-ratified-contract-will-end-24-day-str-05c1526a05/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/orange-county-teamsters-say-have-ratified-contract-will-end-24-day-str-05c1526a05/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:13:05 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Orange County Register</description></item><item><title>Humble Robotics founder Eyal Cohen: self-driving trucks should be built without a driver&#x27;s cab, and regulation is the real brake</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/humble-robotics-founder-eyal-cohen-self-driving-trucks-should-be-built-0bc6995391/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/humble-robotics-founder-eyal-cohen-self-driving-trucks-should-be-built-0bc6995391/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:08:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Humble Robotics, which builds its trucks in San Francisco, has raised a $51 million Series A that brings its total funding to $75 million, according to an interview with founder Eyal Cohen on the MTS podcast. Cohen said the money will go toward building more vehicles, testing them, and running customer pilots to begin moving freight, with pilots targeted &quot;in the next year,&quot; roughly late 2027. He argued that regulation is a major constraint, noting that some truck rules were written about 100 years ago and that a radically redesigned vehicle must still comply with federal, state and local laws.</description></item><item><title>CHP cites truck driver after spotting 20 MPH speed violation and &#x27;numerous&#x27; tire defects on I-5</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/chp-cites-truck-driver-after-spotting-20-mph-speed-violation-and-numer-697b6bd9d3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/chp-cites-truck-driver-after-spotting-20-mph-speed-violation-and-numer-697b6bd9d3/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:59:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>The California Highway Patrol said an officer from its Williams Division stopped a truck on I-5 last week for exceeding the speed limit by more than 20 mph. During the stop, the officer found what the agency called numerous safety problems with the tires on the vehicle combination. The driver was cited for multiple violations and ordered out of service until the equipment was repaired. CHP said troopers will keep targeting speeding and reckless driving in Colusa County. The agency also reminded truckers that California sets a 55 mph limit for truck tractors with three or more axles.</description></item><item><title>Borderlands Mexico: Texas cross-border traffic rises by 400 trucks through Saturday pilot</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/borderlands-mexico-texas-cross-border-traffic-rises-by-400-trucks-thro-03e5744700/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/borderlands-mexico-texas-cross-border-traffic-rises-by-400-trucks-thro-03e5744700/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Small town residents cry for help as immigrant influx fueled by trucking industry has unintended consequences</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/small-town-residents-cry-for-help-as-immigrant-influx-fueled-by-trucki-37a3645a43/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/small-town-residents-cry-for-help-as-immigrant-influx-fueled-by-trucki-37a3645a43/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Fox News</description></item><item><title>Humble Hauler: the 88 km/h electric truck without a cabin</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/humble-hauler-the-88-km-h-electric-truck-without-a-cabin-193134e12e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/humble-hauler-the-88-km-h-electric-truck-without-a-cabin-193134e12e/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:13:30 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Modernet Digital</description></item><item><title>58 kilos of cocaine found on a truck: the driver denies the charges</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/58-kilos-of-cocaine-found-on-a-truck-the-driver-denies-the-charges-d8d66df266/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/58-kilos-of-cocaine-found-on-a-truck-the-driver-denies-the-charges-d8d66df266/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:07:45